From 86b848b14a2ce40fd89614d8f48f90156572ccc4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woodenwillis <william.b@millpex.org>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 01:00:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Add tensor-g4 platform for Google Tensor G4 (zumapro)

The Pixel 9 Pro (caiman) runs a Tensor G4 SoC. This adds a seL4
platform for it so the kernel can be built for the phone, with the
memory map, GIC, timer and debug UART taken from the vendor DTB of
build BP1A.250505.005.

The debug UART at 0x10870000 is compatible "samsung,exynos-uart",
which seL4 did not know. It gets its own driver, registered by that
compatible string, and is added to the hardware.yml serial rule so
hardware_gen can generate UART_PPTR for it.

The GIC redistributor region is given its full DTB size of 0x200000.
The kernel maps only the rule's kernel_size, so the generated header
is unchanged; the DTS stays faithful to the hardware.

RAM is limited to 0x80000000-0xb5000000, below sec_dram, with the
firmware carveouts inside that window marked no-map.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
